000900**************************************************************
001000**                                                          **
001100**D     S C S A S R N M                                     **
001200**                                                          **
001300**D      CSAS CODE RENAME PROGRAM.                          **
001400**D      THIS PROGRAM USES AS INPUT ALL DDAILYTC TC/105s    **
001500**D      (CREATED IN THE CSIS ONLINE CODE RENAME PROGRAM)   **
001600**D      AND RELOADS ALL ENTRIES CONTAINING THE 'OLD'       **
001700**D      MATERIAL CODE WITH THE 'NEW' MATERIAL CODE.        **
001800**D      DATASETS AFFECTED : MMATL-ACCUM, DTRANS.           **
001900**                                                          **
002000**************************************************************
      *C
      *C   7/7/93.    M. L. MITCHELL    REQUEST PAR D. PLUM, #
      *C     REMOVE ALL REFERENCE TO DSET DAAPLFRT (MCFLCA0800).
      *C     ALL LOGICAL, COPYLIB AND WORKING STORAGE REFERENCES
      *C     WERE DELETED.
      *C
      *C   20AUG1993    DAVE PLUM
      *C     IMPROVED THE INFORMATION MOVED TO THE BU-DISPLAY FIELD
      *C     IN THE EVENT OF A BLOWUP.   (GADSDEN EXPERIENCED A BLOWUP
      *C     OF THIS PROGRAM, BUT THERE WAS NOT SUFFICIENT DATA TO
      *C     DETERMINE THE CAUSE OF THE PROBLEM.)
      *C        -NOTE: THE CALLING PROGRAM (TDLYTRNS) UTILIZES THE
      *C               FIELDS BU-DISPLAY-FLD9 (5) AND BU-DISPLAY-FLD (5)
      *C               WHENEVER THIS PROGRAM BLOWS UP, THEREFORE THESE
      *C               2 FIELDS SHOULD NOT BE USED BY THIS PROGRAM.
      *C
      *C   20AUG1993    DAVE PLUM
      *C     HAD TO REWORK THE 61-GET-PUT-DEL-DTRANS PARAGRAPH, SINCE
      *C     AS/400 COBOL NO LONGER ALLOWS YOU TO:
      *C        1) READ A RECORD USING KEY X
      *C        2) CHANGE THE VALUE OF KEY X
      *C        3) REWRITE THE RECORD (INCLUDING THE NEW KEY VALUE)).
      *C     SOME CHANGE WAS MADE TO AS/400 COBOL WHICH NOW CAUSES THE
      *C     REWRITE TO FAIL WITH A FILE STATUS OF 21.
      *C
      *C     WE WILL NOW EMPLOY A STRATEGY WHICH DOES THE FOLLOWING:
      *C        1) READ A RECORD USING KEY X
      *C        2) COPY THE RECORD BUFFER INTO ANOTHER AREA OF WORKING
      *C           STORAGE
      *C        3) DELETE THE RECORD WITH KEY X
      *C        4) WRITE A RECORD TO THE FILE FROM THE ALTERNATE WORKING
      *C           STORAGE BUFFER USING THE NEW KEY VALUE.
      *C
      *C   11SEP1996    DAVE PLUM
      *C     REVISED FOR CENTURY DATABASE CHANGES.
      *C
DP1248*C   04DEC1998    DAVE PLUM
DP1248*C     REVISED TO COMBINE THE MMATL-ACCUM DATA FROM THE OLD CODE
DP1248*C     AND THE NEW CODE, RATHER THAN JUST MOVING THE OLD CODE'S
DP1248*C     VALUES TO THE NEW CODE.  FOR NUMERIC FIELDS THE VALUES FOR
DP1248*C     THE OLD CODE AND NEW CODE WILL BE ADDED TOGETHER.
DP1248*C     ALPHANUMERIC FIELDS WILL CONTINUE TO BE MOVED FROM THE OLD
DP1248*C     CODE TO THE NEW CODE.  (THESE CHANGES ARE TO ACCOMODATE
DP1248*C     THOSE CODE RENAMES WHERE BOTH THE OLD CODE AND THE NEW CODE
DP1248*C     ARE EXISTING CODES WITH DATA IN THE MMATL-ACCUM DATASET.)
DP1248*C     ALSO BEGAN USING THE NEW MMATLACCUM2 COPYLIB MEMBER.
      *C
002100 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
002200 CONFIGURATION SECTION.
002300 SOURCE-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS400.
002400 OBJECT-COMPUTER.  IBM-AS400.
       INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
       FILE-CONTROL.
           SELECT MATLACUM-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA0601
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

           SELECT DTRANS-O
                  ASSIGN TO DATABASE-MCFLCA0701
                  ORGANIZATION IS INDEXED
                    ACCESS MODE IS DYNAMIC
                  RECORD KEY IS EXTERNALLY-DESCRIBED-KEY
                    WITH DUPLICATES
                  FILE STATUS IS FILE-STATUS.

002600 DATA DIVISION.
002700 FILE SECTION.
       FD  MATLACUM-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  MATLACUM-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCA0601.

       FD  DTRANS-O
           LABEL RECORDS ARE STANDARD.
       01  DTRANS-REC-O.
           COPY DDS-ALL-FORMATS OF MCFLCA0701.

002800 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
